SPANS(1)                    UNIX Programmer's Manual                    SPANS(1)

NAME
     spans - the four span kinds and the three rules over them

DESCRIPTION
     Roman text, bold text, italic text, and `a literal run'.

     Rule 2 wants a non-alphanumeric outside a delimiter, so 2**41-1 is
     arithmetic and not a bold run, malloc(2) closes before its parenthesis, and
     (-t) opens after one and closes before another.

     Rule 3's joiner butts two runs together with no space: bsize is one word
     and so is xyz.

     The escapes: a literal * asterisk, a literal ` backtick, a literal \
     backslash, and a | pipe.

     The padded form of a literal run holds a backtick: `a ` b'.

     A marked run may cross a source line inside a paragraph, as this bold run
     does, and so may `a literal run'.
